     "cite": "wiki [[errors-po]] ERR-PO Error Codes > ERR-PO-0412"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**Meaning**  \nUnder Ledgerline 7.2, `ERR-PO-0412` displays `TAX CODE DOES NOT MATCH SUPPLIER COUNTRY (<state>)` [1] (or `[<country_code>]` [3][4]). It is raised by `po_save` on screen `PUR-PO-01` when a purchase order line tax code conflicts with the supplier's recorded country [1][4]. This typically occurs because Ledgerline defaults `VAT20-UK` on order lines, which is invalid for overseas vendors [1]. (The legacy Ledgerline 7.0 message `TAX REGION DOES NOT MATCH SUPPLIER STATE` is superseded [1][3]).\n\n**How to Fix**  \n1. Check the supplier’s recorded country [1].  \n2. Update the line tax code on `PUR-PO-01` [1]:\n   - Non-UK suppliers: select a reverse-charge code such as `VAT20-RC` (standard goods) or `VAT5-RC` (reduced rate) [1][4].\n   - UK suppliers: set to `VAT20-UK` [1].  \n3. Keep the cursor in the line details area and press **F8** to save and recommit [1].  \n4. If the error recurs frequently, notify the purchase ledger team to fix the supplier master profile defaults [1].",
   "cited": [
    1,
    3,
    4
   ],
